# ============================================================================
#  Applied Econometrics (MS) — .gitignore
#
#  This repository is PUBLIC and publishes to GitHub Pages from docs/.
#  Anything committed here is world-readable and stays in history forever.
#
#  Sections are ordered by consequence. Section 1 is a hard deny for anything
#  that could identify a student: only ever add to it, never relax it.
# ============================================================================


# ── 1. Student data — never commit, never push ──────────────────────────────
#
#  Added after four graded assignment submissions were found committed to the
#  public repo and had to be purged from history. `**/submission/` is
#  deliberately broad: it catches submission folders anywhere in the tree,
#  including ones that do not exist yet.
#
#  Keep your local copies wherever you like — git simply will not see them.

roster/
grades/
**/submission/
**/submissions/
**/student-submission/
**/student-submissions/

# Belt and braces: freeze/cache artifacts derived from student files can
# reproduce their names and content.
**/_freeze/**/submission/
**/_freeze/**/student-submission/


# ── 2. Quarto & R build artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────────
#
#  IMPORTANT: docs/ is the published site and MUST stay tracked. Every rule
#  below is scoped to a source directory so that nothing under docs/ is ever
#  ignored — a blanket `**/*_files/` would silently stop new figures from
#  being committed and break the site.

.quarto/
_site/
*.knit.md
*.utf8.md

lectures/**/*_files/
lectures/**/*_cache/
lectures/**/.quarto/
assignments/**/*_files/
assignments/**/*_cache/
exams/**/*_files/
exams/**/*_cache/
research-flow/**/*_files/
research-flow/**/*_cache/

# Rendered HTML in the source tree. The copies that get published live in
# docs/ and are tracked there; these are local render by-products.
lectures/*/*.html
assignments/*/*.html
assignments/*/*/*.html
exams/*/*.html

# ...but the submission form's page is source, not a render by-product. Without
# this the Apps Script project would be missing its only UI file on a fresh
# clone and the form would not deploy.
!assignments/webform/*.html

# Lecture image scratch directory
lectures/*/images/


# ── 3. R / RStudio session state ────────────────────────────────────────────

.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
.Rproj.user/
**/.Rhistory
**/.Rproj.user/


# ── 4. OS and editor noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*~
*.swp


# ── 5. Data files ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#  These stay globally denied rather than path-scoped, on purpose: a roster or
#  gradebook arrives as .csv or .xlsx, and it is usually dropped in whatever
#  directory happens to be open. A global deny means a stray student data file
#  is ignored by default no matter where it lands.
#
#  To publish a specific data file the course genuinely needs, add a negation
#  here rather than deleting the rule, e.g.:
#      !lectures/03-monte-carlo-simulation/example-data.csv

*.csv
*.dta
*.rds
*.rda
*.RData
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.sav

# Exception: the shinylive runtime ships its package index as an .rds inside
# docs/. Without this negation it never gets committed, and the published webr
# apps fail to resolve their packages. docs/ is generated output, so nothing
# sensitive lands here.
!docs/**/*.rds


# ── 6. Source formats not used by the site ──────────────────────────────────
#
#  The course is authored in .qmd. Loose .R and .Rmd files in this repo are
#  older instructor material — including answer keys for assignments 3 and 4
#  that were never meant to be published. Denying these types keeps them out
#  by default. Remove a rule here only after checking what it currently hides:
#      git status --porcelain --ignored | grep '\.Rmd$'

*.R
*.Rmd
*.zip
*.pdf

# Exception: instructor tooling at the top of assignments/ belongs in version
# control. This is scoped to that one directory, so the answer-key .Rmd files
# in assignments/instructor/* stay ignored.
!assignments/*.R

# The course calendar resolver is required to render schedule.qmd and
# syllabus.qmd, so the site cannot build from a fresh clone without it.
!course-dates.R

# The shared ggplot theme every lecture deck sources, and the check that keeps
# the WebR copies of it honest. Without the first one no deck renders from a
# fresh clone.
!lectures/_lecture-theme.R
!lectures/check-lecture-theme.R

/.quarto/

# Built assignment HTML. The built .qmd files under students/<year>/ ARE
# tracked, as the record of what students actually received; the rendered
# HTML is a large regenerable artifact and is not.
assignments/students/*/*/*.html
assignments/students/*/*/*_files/
